WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.707 --> 00:00:09.797
This page mixes practice questions from every week so far into one set, so ideas stay alive instead of fading after their week ends.

2
00:00:09.797 --> 00:00:20.800
Answer, then mark how sure you were. Pick an answer, choose Guessing, Think so, or Sure, then press See how I did. The reveal explains the right answer and what each wrong option gets wrong.

3
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:31.574
Trust the ordering. Questions you have missed before come first. That is deliberate: reviewing what almost stuck is worth more than repeating what already has.

4
00:00:31.574 --> 00:00:42.576
Read the calibration report at the end. It sorts the set into mastered, fragile, confident misses, and growing edges. Confident misses are gold: ideas that feel settled but are not.

5
00:00:42.576 --> 00:00:50.265
Follow the revisit buttons. Every item links back to its home week. Reread the concept, then run another set.

6
00:00:50.265 --> 00:00:57.371
Come back weekly. Two short mixed sets a week beat one long cram. The pool grows as the course does.

7
00:00:57.371 --> 00:01:02.178
Nothing here is scored, recorded, or visible to your professor.

8
00:01:02.178 --> 00:01:08.169
Where next: Run one set now, then revisit the week your confident misses point at.
